NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001118 "L<https://metacpan.org/release/List-MoreUtils>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001119 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001120 "=item * CPAN Search"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001121 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001122 "L<http://search.cpan.org/dist/List-MoreUtils/>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001123 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001124 "=item * Git Repository"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001125 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001126 "L<https://github.com/perl5-utils/List-MoreUtils>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001127 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001128 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001129 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001130 "=head2 Where can I go for help?"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001131 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001132 "If you have a bug report, a patch or a suggestion, please open a new"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001133 "report ticket at CPAN (but please check previous reports first in case"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001134 "your issue has already been addressed) or open an issue on GitHub."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001135 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001136 "Report tickets should contain a detailed description of the bug or"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001137 "enhancement request and at least an easily verifiable way of"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001138 "reproducing the issue or fix. Patches are always welcome, too - and"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001139 "it's cheap to send pull-requests on GitHub. Please keep in mind that"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001140 "code changes are more likely accepted when they're bundled with an"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001141 "approving test."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001142 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001143 "If you think you've found a bug then please read"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001144 "\"How to Report Bugs Effectively\" by Simon Tatham:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001145 "L<http://www.chiark.greenend.org.uk/~sgtatham/bugs.html>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001146 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001147 "=head2 Where can I go for help with a concrete version?"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001148 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001149 "Bugs and feature requests are accepted against the latest version"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001150 "only. To get patches for earlier versions, you need to get an"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001151 "agreement with a developer of your choice - who may or not report the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001152 "issue and a suggested fix upstream (depends on the license you have"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001153 "chosen)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001154 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001155 "=head2 Business support and maintenance"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001156 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001157 "Generally, in volunteered projects, there is no right for support."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001158 "While every maintainer is happy to improve the provided software,"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001159 "spare time is limited."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001160 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001161 "For those who have a use case which requires guaranteed support, one of"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001162 "the maintainers should be hired or contracted.  For business support you"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001163 "can contact Jens via his CPAN email address rehsackATcpan.org. Please"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001164 "keep in mind that business support is neither available for free nor"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001165 "are you eligible to receive any support based on the license distributed"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001166 "with this package."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001167 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001168 "=head1 THANKS"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001169 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001170 "=head2 Tassilo von Parseval"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001171 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001172 "Credits go to a number of people: Steve Purkis for giving me namespace advice"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001173 "and James Keenan and Terrence Branno for their effort of keeping the CPAN"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001174 "tidier by making L<List::Utils> obsolete."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001175 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001176 "Brian McCauley suggested the inclusion of apply() and provided the pure-Perl"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001177 "implementation for it."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001178 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001179 "Eric J. Roode asked me to add all functions from his module C<List::MoreUtil>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001180 "into this one. With minor modifications, the pure-Perl implementations of those"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001181 "are by him."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001182 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001183 "The bunch of people who almost immediately pointed out the many problems with"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001184 "the glitchy 0.07 release (Slaven Rezic, Ron Savage, CPAN testers)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001185 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001186 "A particularly nasty memory leak was spotted by Thomas A. Lowery."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001187 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001188 "Lars Thegler made me aware of problems with older Perl versions."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001189 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001190 "Anno Siegel de-orphaned each_arrayref()."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001191 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001192 "David Filmer made me aware of a problem in each_arrayref that could ultimately"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001193 "lead to a segfault."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001194 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001195 "Ricardo Signes suggested the inclusion of part() and provided the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001196 "Perl-implementation."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001197 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001198 "Robin Huston kindly fixed a bug in perl's MULTICALL API to make the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001199 "XS-implementation of part() work."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001200 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001201 "=head2 Jens Rehsack"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001202 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001203 "Credits goes to all people contributing feedback during the v0.400"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001204 "development releases."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001205 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001206 "Special thanks goes to David Golden who spent a lot of effort to develop"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001207 "a design to support current state of CPAN as well as ancient software"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001208 "somewhere in the dark. He also contributed a lot of patches to refactor"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001209 "the API frontend to welcome any user of List::MoreUtils - from ancient"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001210 "past to recently last used."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001211 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001212 "Toby Inkster provided a lot of useful feedback for sane importer code"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001213 "and was a nice sounding board for API discussions."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001214 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001215 "Peter Rabbitson provided a sane git repository setup containing entire"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001216 "package history."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001217 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001218 "=head1 TODO"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001219 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001220 "A pile of requests from other people is still pending further processing in"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001221 "my mailbox. This includes:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001222 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001223 "=over 4"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001224 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001225 "=item * delete_index"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001226 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001227 "=item * random_item"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001228 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001229 "=item * random_item_delete_index"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001230 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001231 "=item * list_diff_hash"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001232 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001233 "=item * list_diff_inboth"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001234 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001235 "=item * list_diff_infirst"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001236 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001237 "=item * list_diff_insecond"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001238 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001239 "These were all suggested by Dan Muey."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001240 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001241 "=item * listify"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001242 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001243 "Always return a flat list when either a simple scalar value was passed or an"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001244 "array-reference. Suggested by Mark Summersault."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001245 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001246 "=back"
